IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wia-types`
IMPORT `wia-days`
IMPORT `wia-connection`
IMPORT `wia-disconnection`
IMPORT `wia-charges`
IMPORT `wia-goal`

-- Water Industry Act 1991 (UK): independent tests.
-- The expected values come from independent-expectations.md, which was
-- written from the brief and the Act alone. They were not changed to fit the
-- code: a failing assertion records a disagreement.

§ `Independent tests`

hols MEANS LIST (Date 25 12 2025), (Date 26 12 2025), (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 6 4 2026), (Date 4 5 2026), (Date 25 5 2026), (Date 31 8 2026), (Date 28 12 2026)

-- Connection notice by the owner, premises with a building, for a domestic
-- supply, an ordinary main, served on the given day, with the pipe already
-- laid as given, the pipe-laid notice, the counter-notice and the day the
-- conditions were satisfied.
GIVEN served IS A DATE, laid IS A BOOLEAN, pipeNotice IS A MAYBE DATE, counter IS A MAYBE DATE, satisfied IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Connection notice`
conn served laid pipeNotice counter satisfied MEANS
    `Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, served, laid, pipeNotice, counter, satisfied

basic MEANS conn (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING

§§ `Goal 1 — connections`

-- C1
#ASSERT `the duty to connect has arisen for` basic
-- C2 (a proposed building counts as "premises with or for a building")
#ASSERT `the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, (Date 2 3 2026), FALSE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING)
-- C3, C4: a trunk main or a non-domestic main
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, (Date 2 3 2026), TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))
-- C5: not for domestic purposes
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, (Date 2 3 2026), TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING))
-- C6: a condition imposed in time and not yet satisfied
#ASSERT NOT (`the duty to connect has arisen for` (conn (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) NOTHING))
-- C8-C10: notice on 1 Feb 2026, counter-notice on 14, 15 and 16 Feb
#ASSERT `conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 14 2 2026)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT `conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 15 2 2026)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 16 2 2026)) NOTHING))
-- C11: notice on 20 Feb 2026; 6 Mar is the last day, 7 Mar is too late
#ASSERT `conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 20 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 6 3 2026)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 20 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 7 3 2026)) NOTHING))
-- C12: notice on 20 Feb 2028 (leap year); 5 Mar is the last day
#ASSERT `conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 20 2 2028) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2028)) NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`conditions were imposed in time for` (conn (Date 20 2 2028) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 6 3 2028)) NOTHING))
-- A condition imposed late does not stop the duty arising
#ASSERT `the duty to connect has arisen for` (conn (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 16 2 2026)) NOTHING)
-- C13, C14
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` basic EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#EVAL `the last day to connect for` basic
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` basic EQUALS JUST (Date 16 3 2026)
-- C15: conditions imposed in time and satisfied on 10 Mar
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` (conn (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 11 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (conn (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026))) EQUALS JUST (Date 24 3 2026)
-- C16: pipe-laid notice on 28 Feb 2026, pipe not laid when the notice was served
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` (conn (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (JUST (Date 28 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (conn (Date 20 2 2026) FALSE (JUST (Date 28 2 2026)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 21 3 2026)
-- C17: leap year
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` (conn (Date 28 2 2028) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS Date 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (conn (Date 28 2 2028) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 13 3 2028)
-- C18: year end
#ASSERT `the relevant day for` (conn (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS Date 1 1 2027
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (conn (Date 31 12 2026) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 1 2027)
-- No duty, no last day (a trunk main)
#ASSERT `the last day to connect for` (`Connection notice` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, (Date 2 3 2026), TRUE, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- C19-C22: s 48 interest; the rate is 1% of 50p (0.005) per 50p per three months
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 100.30, 0.005, (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 15 8 2026)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 100, 0.005, (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 100, 0.005, (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the interest on my deposit` (`Security deposit` OF 0.40, 0.005, (Date 1 1 2026), (Date 1 1 2027)) EQUALS 0

-- C23-C25: s 106(4)
#ASSERT `the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` (`Sewer notice` OF (Date 10 2 2026), NOTHING) EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF (Date 10 2 2026), JUST (Date 3 3 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF (Date 10 2 2026), JUST (Date 4 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `the refusal was in time for` (`Sewer notice` OF (Date 10 2 2026), JUST (Date 10 2 2026))
#ASSERT `the last day to refuse my sewer connection for` (`Sewer notice` OF (Date 10 2 2028), NOTHING) EQUALS Date 2 3 2028

§§ `Goal 2 — disconnection`

-- The premises, the payment notice day, the payment day, the counter-notice
-- day, whether a judgment is enforceable, whether a settlement is in breach,
-- and the cut-off day. The occupier is liable.
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of premises`, served IS A DATE, pay IS A MAYBE DATE, counter IS A MAYBE DATE, judg IS A BOOLEAN, settle IS A BOOLEAN, cutday IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Non-payment case`
np k served pay counter judg settle cutday MEANS
    `Non-payment case` OF k, TRUE, served, pay, counter, judg, settle, cutday

shop MEANS `premises not listed in Schedule 4A`
home MEANS `a dwelling that is someone's only or principal home`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Non-payment case`
shopCut d MEANS np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE d

-- D1-D5
#ASSERT `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` home
#ASSERT `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` `other premises listed in Schedule 4A`
#ASSERT `the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` `a house in multiple occupation that is someone's only or principal home`
#ASSERT NOT (`the premises are protected by Schedule 4A` shop)
-- D6
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (shopCut (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
-- D7-D9
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (np shop (Date 23 2 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 1 4 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (np shop (Date 23 2 2028) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 1 4 2028)) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2028)
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (np shop (Date 28 12 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 1 2 2027)) EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2027)
-- D10-D12
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (shopCut (Date 9 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (shopCut (Date 10 3 2026))
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (shopCut (Date 11 3 2026))
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (shopCut (Date 9 3 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`cutting off would be an offence for` (shopCut (Date 10 3 2026)))
-- D13: paid on the last day
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 12 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 12 3 2026))
-- D14: paid late on 11 Mar, cut off on 12 Mar (low confidence)
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) (JUST (Date 11 3 2026)) NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 12 3 2026)))
-- D15: a principal home
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (np home (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (np home (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026))
-- D16-D18: a counter-notice on 5 Mar
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `cutting off would be an offence for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026))
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) TRUE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026))
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 5 3 2026)) FALSE TRUE (Date 20 3 2026))
-- D19, D20: a counter-notice on 9 Mar or 10 Mar
#ASSERT NOT (`my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 9 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026)))
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026))
-- D21: a counter-notice served the same day as the notice (low confidence)
#ASSERT `my water may be cut off on the day for` (np shop (Date 2 3 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 2 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE (Date 20 3 2026))
-- Not liable for the charges: no power
#ASSERT `the earliest day my water can be cut off for` (`Non-payment case` OF shop, FALSE, (Date 2 3 2026), NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, (Date 20 3 2026)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- D22, D23
#ASSERT `a limiting device would be an offence for` home
#ASSERT NOT (`a limiting device would be an offence for` shop)

§§ `Goal 3 — charges`

-- Told the undertaker on the given day, left on the given day, next meter
-- reading on the given day, any new occupier's notice; charges by volume.
GIVEN told IS A MAYBE DATE, left IS A DATE, reading IS A DATE, newocc IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Moving out`
mv told left reading newocc MEANS `Moving out` OF told, left, reading, newocc, TRUE

GIVEN told IS A DATE, left IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
inTime told left MEANS `I informed in time for` (mv (JUST told) left (Date 31 12 2027) NOTHING) `, bank holidays` hols

GIVEN m IS A `Moving out`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
lastDay m MEANS `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` m `, bank holidays` hols

-- H1, H2
#ASSERT inTime (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 16 10 2026) (Date 19 10 2026))
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 16 10 2026)) (Date 20 10 2026) (Date 31 12 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- H3, H4: Easter 2026
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 7 4 2026))
#ASSERT inTime (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 8 4 2026)
#ASSERT inTime (Date 1 4 2026) (Date 7 4 2026)
-- H5: Christmas 2026
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 24 12 2026) (Date 29 12 2026))
#ASSERT inTime (Date 24 12 2026) (Date 30 12 2026)
-- H6: late May bank holiday
#ASSERT inTime (Date 22 5 2026) (Date 27 5 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 22 5 2026) (Date 26 5 2026))
-- H7: summer bank holiday
#ASSERT inTime (Date 28 8 2026) (Date 2 9 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 28 8 2026) (Date 1 9 2026))
-- H8: New Year
#ASSERT inTime (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 5 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 2 1 2026))
-- H9: told on a Saturday, left the second working day after
-- (this reading differs from the brief)
#ASSERT NOT (inTime (Date 17 10 2026) (Date 20 10 2026))
-- H10
#ASSERT inTime (Date 17 10 2026) (Date 21 10 2026)
-- H11: unmeasured charges
#ASSERT `the last day I can be charged for after leaving` (`Moving out` OF (JUST (Date 9 7 2026)), (Date 10 7 2026), (Date 30 9 2026), NOTHING, FALSE) `, bank holidays` hols EQUALS NOTHING
-- H12-H14
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 9 7 2026)) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 6 8 2026)
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 9 7 2026)) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) (JUST (Date 20 7 2026))) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 7 2026)
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 9 7 2026)) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 1 8 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2026)
-- H15: told after leaving
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 15 7 2026)) (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 8 2026)
-- H16, H17: month ends
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) (Date 30 1 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT lastDay (mv (JUST (Date 1 2 2028)) (Date 31 1 2028) (Date 30 6 2028) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2028)
-- H18: never told; the next normal reading after leaving is 30 Sep
#ASSERT lastDay (mv NOTHING (Date 10 7 2026) (Date 30 9 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 9 2026)

-- H19-H22: s 62 notice
GIVEN s IS A DATE, e IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
s62 s e MEANS `the last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` (`Section 62 notice` OF s, e) `, bank holidays` hols

#ASSERT s62 (Date 19 10 2026) (Date 19 10 2026) EQUALS Date 21 10 2026
#ASSERT s62 (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 3 4 2026) EQUALS Date 8 4 2026
#ASSERT s62 (Date 2 4 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS Date 30 4 2026
#ASSERT s62 (Date 24 12 2026) (Date 24 12 2026) EQUALS Date 30 12 2026

-- Meters. Fields: home, unmeasured, not practicable, unreasonable expense,
-- measured began, first notice, remain consumer, s 144A(7) met,
-- notice or consent, occupation changed with no charges demanded.
GIVEN began IS A MAYBE DATE, first IS A BOOLEAN, remain IS A BOOLEAN, seven IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Meter case`
rev began first remain seven MEANS `Meter case` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, began, first, remain, seven, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN hm IS A BOOLEAN, unmeasured IS A BOOLEAN, notprac IS A BOOLEAN, ue IS A BOOLEAN, consent IS A BOOLEAN, changed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Meter case`
mc hm unmeasured notprac ue consent changed MEANS `Meter case` OF hm, unmeasured, notprac, ue, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, consent, changed

-- M1, M2
#ASSERT `I may require a meter for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`I may require a meter for` (mc FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`I may require a meter for` (mc TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- M3, M4
#ASSERT `the undertaker must meter me for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker must meter me for` (mc TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker must meter me for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- M5-M8
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 1 3 2027)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 29 2 2028)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 1 1 2026)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2026)
-- Further month ends: 31 Jan and 28 Feb
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 31 1 2026)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 30 1 2027)
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 28 2 2027)) TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST (Date 27 2 2028)
-- M10: a previous notice, still the consumer, (7) not met
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The giver is no longer the consumer and (7) is not met
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- M11: (7) met
#ASSERT `the last day to revoke my meter for` (rev (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2027)
-- B1-B8
#ASSERT NOT (`the undertaker may impose a meter for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (mc TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the undertaker may impose a meter for` (mc FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `Top-level goal`

-- The default export, with only the s 62 notice and the non-payment facts given
topcase MEANS `Water customer case` OF hols, NOTHING, NOTHING, NOTHING, JUST (shopCut (Date 10 3 2026)), NOTHING, JUST (`Section 62 notice` OF (Date 2 4 2026), (Date 3 4 2026)), NOTHING
top MEANS `the water customer position for` topcase
#ASSERT top's `earliest day my water can be cut off` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT top's `water may be cut off on the day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT top's `last day I can be charged for after my s 62 notice` EQUALS JUST (Date 8 4 2026)
#ASSERT top's `duty to connect has arisen` EQUALS NOTHING
